{"uid":"6393db9696c6b873","name":"test_a_settled_obligation_supplied_truncated_retires_the_full_filing_too","fullName":"tests.test_confirmed_petition_not_resurfaced#test_a_settled_obligation_supplied_truncated_retires_the_full_filing_too","historyId":"811088f1700e07b5b66a9d7dc01f50b8","time":{"start":1791881189072,"stop":1791881189079,"duration":7},"description":"`_obligation_confirmed`'s normalised substring-either-direction rule\n    is reused verbatim for the SETTLED set, which is what makes the real\n    defect's two wordings of one obligation retire together: `deck-phase4`'s\n    ledger held the same obligation twice, once cut at 56 characters because\n    its `**Obligation**:` field was hard-wrapped and `_FIELD_RE` captures a\n    single line. Both directions are pinned (ledger shorter than filing, and\n    filing shorter than ledger) because either can happen depending on which\n    channel wrapped. The negative control in the same node keeps the rule\n    bounded: an unrelated obligation in the same file still renders, so this\n    pins fuzzy matching, not \"matches everything\".","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>_obligation_confirmed</code>'s normalised substring-either-direction rule<br />\nis reused verbatim for the SETTLED set, which is what makes the real<br />\ndefect's two wordings of one obligation retire together: <code>deck-phase4</code>'s<br />\nledger held the same obligation twice, once cut at 56 characters because<br />\nits <code>**Obligation**:</code> field was hard-wrapped and <code>_FIELD_RE</code> captures a<br />\nsingle line. Both directions are pinned (ledger shorter than filing, and<br />\nfiling shorter than ledger) because either can happen depending on which<br />\nchannel wrapped. The negative control in the same node keeps the rule<br />\nbounded: an unrelated obligation in the same file still renders, so this<br />\npins fuzzy matching, not &quot;matches everything&quot;.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBr